106b. Is deeply concerned by the findings of the FRA report1a that the ‘near-permanent deployment of special security measures – including heavily armed guards – at schools, synagogues and community centres’ has become a necessity, and that Jewish organisations are forced to use their ‘valuable human and financial resources to provide increased security’; stresses that it is completely unacceptable in a democratic society that a specific community must live under such permanent threat;

---

1a EU Agency for Fundamental Rights, ‘Jewish People’s Experiences and Perceptions of Antisemitism’, 2024, p. 17.
